# Build context for backend/Dockerfile.
#
# The `.env` line is a security control, not an optimisation: that file holds live JWT
# and OIDC signing secrets plus OAuth client credentials, and a `COPY . .` would bake it
# into a layer that survives deleting the file in a later one. Secrets reach this image
# only as runtime environment variables.

# Produced inside the image from the lockfile. A host node_modules also carries
# platform-specific binaries that would not run on alpine.
node_modules
dist

# Secrets and local key material. Production supplies the signing key via
# OIDC_RSA_PRIVATE_KEY / OIDC_RSA_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH, never a baked-in PEM.
.env
.env.*
cert

# Tests and their helpers are kept out of the context so `tsc` never emits them into
# dist/ — cheaper and harder to get wrong than deleting compiled tests afterwards.
**/*.test.ts
src/common/testing
# Benchmarks depend on the test harness above and are development-only. Keeping them
# out also prevents their compiled output from entering the production image.
scripts/bench-*.ts

# No role at runtime.
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
*.md
*.tsbuildinfo
scripts/*.sh
